{"text": "STATE OF CALIFORNIA\n\nKnowledge Testing Modernization to Enhance AKTE\n\nDIGITAL INFORMATION BRANCH * CUSTOMER SERVICES DIVISION + \u00a9 2021 STATE OF CALIFORNIA, DEPARTMENT OF MOTOR VEHICLES. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED.\n\nEffective Date: April 27, 2021\n\nNew Information\nThe Knowledge Testing Modernization project will make enhancements to the following\nareas of the Automated Knowledge Testing Enhancement (AKTE) system:\ne Knowledge test languages\ne Knowledge test questions\ne Audio knowledge tests\n\nKnowledge Test Languages\nCurrently, the AKTE system offers noncommercial driver\u2019s license (DL) knowledge tests in\n32 foreign languages. The Knowledge Testing Modernization project will reduce the tests\nfrom 32 to the 7 languages required by the Dymally-Alatorre Language Services Act:\nEN-English\nSP-Spanish\nAN-Armenian\nCH-Chinese\nHI-Hindi\nPU-Punyjabi\ne VI-Vietnamese\nNOTE: Until programming is in place, the language selection screen will continue to\ndisplay all 32 languages. However, if the customer selects a language other than the 7\nDymally-Alatorre languages, the renewal test will be administered in English.\n\nKnowledge Test Questions\nCurrently, the noncommercial DL renewal knowledge test consists of 18 questions. The\nKnowledge Testing Modernization project will increase the number to 25 questions.\nConsequently, the current fail threshold will be increased from 3 to 5.\n\nAudio Knowledge Tests\nThis new enhancement will temporarily remove the audio knowledge test option.\nIf the applicant requests additional accommodations to attempt the knowledge test, such as\nrequiring the test questions and answers to be read aloud, offer to schedule a Person-to-\nPerson (PTP).\n\nFollow the current procedures for scheduling and administering PTP tests.\n\nNOTE: PTP tests can only be conducted in the same languages that are available on the\nTouchScreen Terminal (TST) for the corresponding knowledge test.\n\nElectronically distributed 04/27/2021 Page | of 2\nContact\u2014CSD Help Desk",
